export anchor SplitFlapTimetableStyle:
    number: 77
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Split-flap timetable
    idea: The dashboard is a railway departures hall in light grey, where projects leave from numbered platforms, key words are set in split-flap character cells and the remarks column says whether each one is on time.
    base: light
    palette:
        hall: #e9eaea, the page
        board: #cfd3d6, board housings and the focused list row
        frame: #858b90, the 6px housing frame and row rules
        flap: #fbfbf8, character cells
        ink: #141618, flap letters, buttons and sign borders
        grey: #474d52, captions and the calling at lines
        platformBlue: #1d3f8f, platform number squares and the current nav sign
        noticeYellow: #ffcc33, the customer notice strip and the focus outline
        green: #17663a, On track with a solid disc
        amber: #8a4d00, At risk with a solid triangle
        red: #b01c1c, Behind and the overdue count with a solid square
    type:
        Flap text uses ui-monospace, SF Mono, Menlo, Consolas in bold caps,
        one letter per cell. Each cell is 0.92em wide with a 2px gap, a 2px
        radius, a thin dark seam across the middle and a 1px grey lip below.
        The full text is kept for screen readers and the cells are hidden
        from them. Flap sizes are 26px for the greeting, 34px for counts,
        17px in departure rows, 15px for arrival times and 14px in list
        rows. Signs and body use Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, board
        titles 18px at 800, captions 11px bold caps tracked 0.16em.
    layout:
        A station header holds a ring and bar roundel with Brightwork, nav
        as six white signs each with a black number square, Home inverted
        blue, then a FIND search with a ruled label, a black New project
        button, a bell with 3 and Signed in Mara Okafor. A grey housing with
        a 6px frame shows the greeting and the date in flap cells and a
        yellow Customer notice strip with a loudspeaker saying 4 tasks are
        overdue and to check Billing migration first. Four small housings
        show the counts in flap cells, the overdue one in red. The
        Departures board is a table with Due, Destination with calling at
        and the team, a blue platform square, progress in mono with tasks
        below, and Remarks with a shape, the status in flap cells and an
        italic note such as running on time, expect delays or delayed. Below
        sit an Arrivals board for activity with flap times, and a chart
        board where each day is a column of small cells, one per task, open
        cells last week and filled cells this week. At 375px each departure
        becomes a stacked block and arrivals put the time above the text.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 9 to 12px cell padding in rows and 14 to 16px between boards.
    density: Medium high. Long boards with one row per project.
    corners: Square signs, 4px housings and 2px flap cells.
    borders: A 6px grey frame round each board, 2px rules between rows and 2px ink on signs and fields.
    shadows: A flat 3px lip under each housing with no blur.
    icons:
        Station pictograms in solid ink, a train face, an arrow and bars.
        Remarks use a disc for On track, a triangle for At risk and a square
        for Behind beside the flap word.
    focus: A 3px notice yellow outline with a 5px ink ring outside it.
    tone: A station announcer, such as Departures, calling at Design, running on time, expect delays and Customer notice.
